s pressure on the landlord, (3) it preserves my ♣2 (the strongest card) for a critical counter-play when the landlord plays their final cards, and (4) it keeps my pair of 8s intact for potential later use. Passing here would be extremely risky as it could hand victory to the landlord.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♦J"]}'}
